Feature: Checkout Card Payment, Promo, and Stock Validation Regression
  As an e-commerce customer
  I want my card payment, applied promo code, and stock availability to be processed accurately and securely at checkout
  So that I am charged the correct amount, my order reflects the true payment outcome, and my card data is protected

  Background:
    Given the customer has added eligible items to their cart
    And the customer has proceeded to the checkout page with card payment selected

  @smoke @critical @risk-critical
  Scenario Outline: Order status reflects the payment gateway's authorization outcome
    Given a customer has submitted a card payment for their order
    When the payment gateway returns an authorization result of "<gateway_result>"
    Then the order status is set to "<expected_order_status>"

    Examples:
      | gateway_result | expected_order_status |
      | approved       | Confirmed              |
      | declined       | Payment Failed         |
      | timeout        | Pending Retry          |

  @regression @risk-high
  Scenario: Stock depletion after cart lock triggers a payment reversal and consistent order state
    Given a customer has locked their cart with sufficient stock available
    When the last unit of the locked item goes out of stock before payment capture completes
    Then the payment authorization is reversed
    And the order status reflects that the order could not be fulfilled

  @security @risk-high
  Scenario: Card verification value and card number are masked throughout the checkout journey
    Given a customer is on the checkout payment page with a saved or newly entered card
    When the customer completes the card payment step
    Then the card verification value is not displayed, returned in any API response, or written to logs at any checkout step
    And the card number is shown only in masked form using the first six and last four digits

  @negative @security @risk-medium
  Scenario: Payment is rejected when the card verification value contains invalid characters
    Given a customer is entering card details at checkout
    When the customer submits a card verification value containing non-numeric or oversized input
    Then the payment submission is rejected
    And the customer sees a validation message without any indication of the underlying system error

  @regression @risk-high
  Scenario: Duplicate capture is prevented when a card payment is retried after a network timeout
    Given a customer submitted a card payment that experienced a network timeout before confirmation
    When the customer retries the same payment
    Then only one capture is recorded against the order
    And no duplicate debit occurs

  @regression @risk-medium
  Scenario: Final bank debit matches the recalculated cart total after a price change following promo application
    Given a customer has applied a valid promo code to their cart
    When the price of an item in the cart changes before payment capture
    Then the cart total is recalculated to include the promo discount and the updated price
    And the amount debited from the customer's bank account equals the recalculated cart total

  @boundary @edge-case @risk-medium
  Scenario Outline: Promo code eligibility is enforced at the minimum cart value threshold
    Given a customer's cart total is "<cart_total_relative_to_minimum>" the promo code's minimum eligible value
    When the customer applies the promo code at checkout
    Then the promo discount is "<expected_outcome>"

    Examples:
      | cart_total_relative_to_minimum | expected_outcome |
      | one unit below                 | rejected          |
      | exactly at                     | applied           |
      | one unit above                 | applied           |

